544
00:33:01,180 --> 00:33:08,380
It's the smallest of all seeds, but when it's grown, it's taller than the garden plants and becomes a tree,

545
00:33:08,380 --> 00:33:13,060
so that the birds of the sky will come and nest in its branches.

546
00:33:13,060 --> 00:33:15,420
He told them another parable.

547
00:33:15,740 --> 00:33:22,920
The kingdom of heaven is like leaven that a woman took and mixed into 50 pounds of flour until all of it was leaven.

548
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:28,500
Jesus told the crowds these things in parables, and he did not tell them anything without a parable,

549
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:31,240
so that what was spoken through the prophet might be fulfilled.

550
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:37,080
I will open my mouth in parables, and I will declare things kept secret from the foundation of the world.

551
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:39,220
This is the word of the Lord.

552
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:50,320
Now, before we jump into the exposition of the text,

553
00:33:50,320 --> 00:33:55,520
Jesus taught in parables to invite his listeners to go deeper, beyond the surface,

554
00:33:55,520 --> 00:33:59,560
to encounter and be confronted with the mystery of God's kingdom.

555
00:33:59,560 --> 00:34:03,640
A couple of verses before this, right, remember last week, Jesus says,

556
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,420
let anyone who has ears listen.

557
00:34:05,420 --> 00:34:10,300
And what Jesus is doing is inviting us in to discover what God is revealing.

558
00:34:10,900 --> 00:34:16,460
Like Kent talked about last week, parables were meant to hit the ears of those who were even actively plugging their own ears.

559
00:34:16,460 --> 00:34:18,840
Let anyone who has ears listen.

560
00:34:18,840 --> 00:34:23,820
It's the same language I use with my kids when they do, when I say something, they don't do it.

561
00:34:23,820 --> 00:34:25,600
Right?

562
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:26,960
Church, this is us.

563
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:28,920
So, did you hear what I said?

564
00:34:28,920 --> 00:34:34,100
I'm assuming, children, you did not hear because you did not do.

565
00:34:34,100 --> 00:34:37,680
See, God, I think, works in the same way with us.

566
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:42,660
The true response to hearing is doing something about it.

567
00:34:42,660 --> 00:34:46,700
True response, true listening requires a response.

568
00:34:46,700 --> 00:34:48,140
Because here's what I've learned.

569
00:34:48,140 --> 00:34:57,340
Jesus' lessons and parables often confront me and my flesh on the direction and initiative that I want to take versus the truth of the kingdom of God.

570
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:03,560
See, in areas I want to be in control and tell things to God, like, sure, sure we don't try it this way.

571
00:35:03,560 --> 00:35:08,560
The parables confront me and say, boy, play a role.

572
00:35:08,560 --> 00:35:10,540
I told you what the kingdom of God is like.

573
00:35:10,540 --> 00:35:12,180
Are you being honest to that?

574
00:35:13,520 --> 00:35:16,080
Which leads us into the first part of our passage today.

575
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,120
The mustard seed.

576
00:35:17,120 --> 00:35:20,320
Small, insignificant, unstoppable.

577
00:35:20,320 --> 00:35:24,220
If you've spent any time around church, you've probably heard of the parable of the mustard seed.

578
00:35:24,220 --> 00:35:35,200
And I've probably, and again, real people realize, right, I've probably read past this ten times and didn't stop at four verses that I think have huge implications.

579
00:35:37,200 --> 00:35:41,640
My wife, Samantha, actually has a beautiful ring with a tiny mustard seed set inside of it.

580
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:44,640
And I thought about that as I was kind of preparing the message today.

581
00:35:44,640 --> 00:35:53,120
And that's what the Holy Spirit put in my heart, that this tiny mustard seed, one of the, it's a reminder of this teaching and also the one on faith, right, that we're all familiar with.

582
00:35:53,120 --> 00:35:58,620
But the reminder that even the smallest beginnings in God's hands have unstoppable potential.

583
00:35:58,620 --> 00:36:04,600
And Jesus says here, the kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed.

584
00:36:05,940 --> 00:36:09,280
So again, to get us all in the same mindset, the what is like a mustard seed?

585
00:36:09,280 --> 00:36:11,320
The kingdom of heaven.

586
00:36:11,320 --> 00:36:12,840
That's important.

587
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:16,520
Because Jesus isn't just giving us a cute story about seeds and plants.

588
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:20,320
He's telling us what his kingdom is like.

589
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:26,380
And I worry for sometimes for those of us that grew up in church, right, I'm preaching to myself here.

590
00:36:26,820 --> 00:36:31,700
That we either have no real working definition of what the kingdom of heaven is.

591
00:36:33,700 --> 00:36:40,260
Or, like Jesus' original audience, we've quietly built up our own expectations about what it should be.

592
00:36:40,260 --> 00:36:46,320
We're unwilling to let the words of Jesus conform that understanding to what he says it is.

593
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:52,820
Just real quick, before I go any further, I may slip up, so I want to get on stable ground with you guys.

594
00:36:53,220 --> 00:36:59,480
You'll hear me use the phrases kingdom of heaven and kingdom of God somewhat interchangeably.

595
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:07,880
Matthew, kind of our source text today, tends to say kingdom of heaven out of reverence for God's name because he's speaking to a primarily Jewish audience.

596
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:10,200
But he's talking about the same beautiful reality.

597
00:37:10,200 --> 00:37:14,680
That the rule and reign of God breaking into the world through Jesus.

598
00:37:16,040 --> 00:37:18,400
And that's where we have to be careful, church.

599
00:37:18,400 --> 00:37:21,880
I'm going to say, I already said I'm going to step up, so I might as well do it.

600
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:22,400
Yeah.

601
00:37:22,400 --> 00:37:25,240
This is where we have to be careful.

602
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:36,700
I think we need, need, that's important, we need to build a theology of the kingdom of understanding what God is doing.

603
00:37:36,700 --> 00:37:38,000
We need to do that, right?

604
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:40,540
You heard me.

605
00:37:40,540 --> 00:37:45,080
Yep, we need, I think we need to do the work of building a kingdom theology.

606
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:51,920
We need to do the work of building a kingdom theology because we need to understand and see how God operates and works.

607
00:37:51,920 --> 00:37:54,020
And we pray this in the Lord's Prayer.

608
00:37:54,020 --> 00:37:56,220
Your kingdom come.

609
00:37:56,220 --> 00:37:58,600
Your will be done.

610
00:37:58,600 --> 00:38:02,820
I think we have no expectation for what God's kingdom can look like.

611
00:38:02,820 --> 00:38:09,960
We easily become pessimistic and even depressed around the current affairs because we don't know what to do with them.

612
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:11,400
In light of Jesus.

613
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:15,480
We can't see kingdom work because we don't know where to look.

614
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:20,320
Because we have no established framework for it.

615
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:22,360
But here's the tension.

616
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:23,280
Tons of tension.

617
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:28,340
At the same time, you need to do the work of building a kingdom theology.

618
00:38:28,340 --> 00:38:35,380
You also need to hold it so loosely that when Jesus tells us a parable, he can reframe us, not the other way around.

619
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:43,300
We should do the work of building a kingdom theology because I believe kingdom understanding is our kingdom ethic.

620
00:38:43,300 --> 00:38:45,040
Corey, what do you mean by that?

621
00:38:45,520 --> 00:38:51,000
I mean that the way you and I understand the kingdom of God drives our Christian ethics.

622
00:38:51,000 --> 00:38:52,380
Think about that.

623
00:38:52,380 --> 00:38:59,760
In other words, what we believe about God's rule and reign will shape how we live it out.

624
00:39:00,920 --> 00:39:07,240
If we think God's kingdom is about power, control, and being on top, that's how we're going to live it out.

625
00:39:08,040 --> 00:39:15,300
But if we believe the kingdom is about sacrifice, service, love, and small act of obedience, then that's how we're going to live it out.

626
00:39:16,460 --> 00:39:19,900
Because kingdom understanding is our kingdom ethic.

627
00:39:19,900 --> 00:39:25,160
But Jesus says the kingdom is like a mustard seed.

628
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:26,640
What does that mean?

629
00:39:26,640 --> 00:39:34,100
Small and slow, hidden and humble, yet it transforms everything from the inside out.

630
00:39:34,100 --> 00:39:35,140
Does that make sense?

631
00:39:35,140 --> 00:39:35,580
My kingdom?

632
00:39:35,580 --> 00:39:36,560
Oh, jiving?

633
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:37,500
Tracking?

634
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:44,860
Because if we come to these parables with no thought of what the kingdom of heaven is or how it operates, these parables do little to shape us.

635
00:39:44,860 --> 00:39:46,360
They are just a word count.

636
00:39:47,020 --> 00:39:48,240
They're just reading, right?

637
00:39:48,240 --> 00:39:50,700
They do nothing to shape our understanding of the kingdom.

638
00:39:50,700 --> 00:39:56,040
But on the other hand, if we come to the parables thinking we already know how the kingdom of heaven should work,

639
00:39:56,040 --> 00:40:01,240
we might miss the small, surprising, hidden ways that God actually chooses to move.

640
00:40:01,240 --> 00:40:07,800
Jesus knew this, so he utilizes the tools of parables to get past our defenses

641
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:12,700
and present the truest information about what the kingdom of heaven is actually like.

642
00:40:12,700 --> 00:40:14,780
N.T. Wright says this.

643
00:40:14,920 --> 00:40:17,480
My wife laughed at me because I quote N.T. Wright all the time.

644
00:40:17,480 --> 00:40:20,060
But Jesus' stories are not just good advice.

645
00:40:20,060 --> 00:40:28,160
They are designed to break open worldviews and reconstruct them around the reality of God's reign.

646
00:40:30,160 --> 00:40:34,700
One of the most surprising pictures Jesus gives is the parable of the mustard seed.

647
00:40:34,700 --> 00:40:39,100
But I want you to remember back to last week what Kent said, don't remember the parables by their names.

648
00:40:39,100 --> 00:40:42,140
Then we get into a very shallow understanding of the parables.

649
00:40:42,700 --> 00:40:43,880
So what do we need to do?

650
00:40:43,880 --> 00:40:44,900
Slow down.

651
00:40:44,900 --> 00:40:46,200
Let's take a closer look.

652
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:53,520
When we do, I think we'll realize that the teaching of Jesus is something far more radical than you and I usually realize with first claim.

653
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:58,160
See, most scholars believe Jesus is referring to the black mustard plant,

654
00:40:58,160 --> 00:40:59,760
which was common around the Middle East.

655
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:01,400
And black mustard seeds are tiny.

656
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:03,020
They're about one to two millimeters.

657
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:07,300
And they would have been known by the audience among some of the smallest seeds.

658
00:41:07,300 --> 00:41:12,200
I'm not getting into a literal discussion about if it's the smallest seed.

659
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:13,340
That's not what Jesus is meaning.

660
00:41:14,260 --> 00:41:19,180
But despite its size, the mustard plant can grow to six to 12 feet tall in just a season.

661
00:41:19,180 --> 00:41:25,120
But I think in our minds, we picture, just like Jesus' words, we picture this tree.

662
00:41:25,120 --> 00:41:31,880
But in reality, the mustard seed is more like a giant, unruly shrub than a neatly planted tree.

663
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:34,040
And here's the key.

664
00:41:34,040 --> 00:41:39,620
While the mustard plant grew commonly in the wild, no self-respecting farmer would have planted one.

665
00:41:41,300 --> 00:41:47,140
So, because it's invasive, it spreads aggressively by seed and root.

666
00:41:47,140 --> 00:41:50,580
And once planted, it will quickly dominate a small plot of land.

667
00:41:50,580 --> 00:41:52,860
Doesn't sound like something a farmer's going to plant.

668
00:41:52,860 --> 00:41:56,680
See, Jesus isn't giving a lesson in botany.

669
00:41:56,680 --> 00:42:01,980
He's describing the outrageous, even disruptive growth of the kingdom of God.

670
00:42:01,980 --> 00:42:08,200
See, this tiny, unimpressive seed, it will take over the garden.

671
00:42:09,600 --> 00:42:20,940
See, for Jesus to say the kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed that a man took and sowed in his field would have sounded shocking, counterintuitive, and even disruptive to his audience.

672
00:42:20,940 --> 00:42:23,640
Tell us more, because that's not how we do it.

673
00:42:23,640 --> 00:42:25,080
So that's problem one, right?

674
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:30,180
No sane farmer listening would have intentionally planted a mustard seed.

675
00:42:31,020 --> 00:42:34,440
Jesus wants us to notice the problems and focus our attention there.

676
00:42:34,440 --> 00:42:42,780
It's almost like Jesus is saying, and I tried to make this, like, modern reader, 21st century Virginian lingo.

677
00:42:42,780 --> 00:42:45,420
I don't make it too hillbilly, so you're welcome.

678
00:42:45,420 --> 00:42:54,900
The kingdom of God is like planting dandelions and crabgrass in your pristine, well-manicured suburban lawns.

679
00:42:56,300 --> 00:42:57,320
Would you do that?

680
00:42:57,320 --> 00:42:58,920
No, you would.

681
00:42:58,920 --> 00:42:59,940
No, I'm not doing that.

682
00:42:59,940 --> 00:43:01,260
Why would anybody do that?

683
00:43:01,260 --> 00:43:03,200
But, I mean, the kids will love to blow them.

684
00:43:03,200 --> 00:43:04,040
It's going to look really cute.

685
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:05,200
You're going to love it.

686
00:43:05,200 --> 00:43:06,040
So try it.

687
00:43:06,040 --> 00:43:14,820
Or, in my realm, in my line of work, the kingdom of heaven is like kudzu or bamboo.

688
00:43:14,820 --> 00:43:16,940
You can't stop it.

689
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:20,060
And once it sprouts, it spreads wide.

690
00:43:20,060 --> 00:43:22,300
Once it's rooted, good luck trying to get rid of it.

691
00:43:22,300 --> 00:43:22,820
It's there.

692
00:43:22,820 --> 00:43:29,420
The kingdom of God, Jesus says, is like an invasive plant.

693
00:43:29,420 --> 00:43:33,460
Wild, disruptive, unstoppable.

694
00:43:33,460 --> 00:43:38,340
It will spread beyond our fences, beyond our control, and beyond you and I's expectations.

695
00:43:38,340 --> 00:43:43,680
See, this is what most modern readers miss, and I am among the modern readers.

696
00:43:44,860 --> 00:43:53,140
But the people listening to Jesus would have understood what the mustard seed produces is an intrusive weed that will take over everything.

697
00:43:53,140 --> 00:43:59,240
It's not just that Jesus says, the kingdom's like a weed that farmers don't want.

698
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:00,860
No, it's worse.

699
00:44:01,560 --> 00:44:10,520
He's saying the kingdom is like an invasive force that overwhelms useful crops, monopolizes the moisture, outgrows its competitors, and steals the sunshine.

700
00:44:10,520 --> 00:44:15,780
Jesus wants his listeners to feel uncomfortable with that.

701
00:44:15,780 --> 00:44:22,640
Because the kingdom of God doesn't grow through respectability or careful human management.

702
00:44:24,240 --> 00:44:30,420
It invades, it disrupts, and it spreads wherever it wants.

703
00:44:30,420 --> 00:44:34,940
The kingdom of heaven isn't a curated garden.

704
00:44:34,940 --> 00:44:37,740
It's a wild, unstoppable force.

705
00:44:37,740 --> 00:44:40,420
Folks, hear me.

706
00:44:42,920 --> 00:44:47,240
The kingdom of heaven is not a safe place.

707
00:44:47,240 --> 00:44:50,440
It's unpredictable.

708
00:44:50,440 --> 00:44:52,440
It cannot be harnessed.

709
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:54,560
It cannot be domesticated.

710
00:44:54,560 --> 00:44:56,720
It is risky, and it is dangerous.

711
00:44:56,720 --> 00:44:59,140
And I'm stepping on my own toes here.

712
00:44:59,140 --> 00:45:05,380
The kingdom of heaven is unpredictable, unharnessed, risky, dangerous.

713
00:45:05,540 --> 00:45:09,620
Friends, I fear that comfort and privilege have made us complacent.

714
00:45:09,620 --> 00:45:15,100
We've been sold a version of Christianity that says, God wants you to be comfortable.

715
00:45:15,100 --> 00:45:21,640
And I want you to read the Gospels in light of this message, especially after Jesus tells a parable.

716
00:45:21,640 --> 00:45:25,600
Be prepared to give up everything, including your life.

717
00:45:25,600 --> 00:45:29,260
Sell everything you have and give it to the poor.

718
00:45:29,260 --> 00:45:33,080
Take up your cross and follow me.

719
00:45:34,400 --> 00:45:38,520
Folks, in real biblical Christianity, everything is on the table.

720
00:45:38,520 --> 00:45:41,380
No one leaves unchanged.

721
00:45:41,380 --> 00:45:46,940
The kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed.

722
00:45:46,940 --> 00:45:57,180
And yet, here we are, dividing over elections, shouting at each other online, measuring influence by who sits in the seat of power.

723
00:45:58,580 --> 00:46:05,380
All while the true king says, the kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed.

724
00:46:07,120 --> 00:46:10,000
Now, some good pastoral guardrails.

725
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:12,240
Because I think we can get into a mindset.

726
00:46:12,240 --> 00:46:14,300
And this is why we do things in community, right?

727
00:46:14,300 --> 00:46:19,560
While I believe all those things about the kingdom of heaven are true and real,

728
00:46:19,560 --> 00:46:24,460
one thing I am not saying about the kingdom of heaven is it is chaotic.

729
00:46:25,540 --> 00:46:30,700
God, throughout the narrative of Scripture, constantly restrains and conquers the chaos monsters.

730
00:46:31,180 --> 00:46:34,160
The mustard seed is not a chaotic picture.

731
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:38,960
But instead, one that begs the question of us.

732
00:46:40,100 --> 00:46:43,960
Do we allow the kingdom of heaven to disrupt our lives like a mustard seed?

733
00:46:43,960 --> 00:46:51,120
What if that seed pushed us out of our comfort zones and into neighborhoods we'd rather avoid?

734
00:46:53,040 --> 00:46:57,180
What if it pushed us into radical generosity that makes no worldly sense?

735
00:46:57,180 --> 00:47:05,660
What if instead of managing our faith, this is me, what if instead of managing our faith like a garden, we'd let it uproot us?

736
00:47:05,660 --> 00:47:13,260
What I'm saying, folks, and hear me, the kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed.

737
00:47:13,260 --> 00:47:16,200
I feel like the ShamWow guy now.

738
00:47:16,200 --> 00:47:18,200
But wait, there's more.

739
00:47:19,720 --> 00:47:23,560
The problem, too, the mustard seed really doesn't grow into a tree, right?

740
00:47:23,560 --> 00:47:26,060
We have this picture and expectation in our mind.

741
00:47:26,060 --> 00:47:36,200
We tend to think of something when Jesus references trees, we think of something majestic, towering, like oak trees here in the valley or giant sequoias or redwoods out in the west coast.

742
00:47:36,200 --> 00:47:40,740
Especially when we tend to think of a picture of the kingdom of heaven.

743
00:47:40,740 --> 00:47:44,860
What picture would God use to describe the kingdom of heaven?

744
00:47:44,860 --> 00:47:48,380
But a mustard seed really doesn't grow into that kind of tree.

745
00:47:48,700 --> 00:47:50,680
Again, it's a big shrub.

746
00:47:50,680 --> 00:47:53,420
It's a messy, sprawling bush that takes over.

747
00:47:53,420 --> 00:47:56,280
So the mustard seed isn't what we expect.

748
00:47:56,280 --> 00:48:03,080
What does Jesus mean by a tree that the birds of the air nest in its branches?

749
00:48:03,080 --> 00:48:05,000
So we beg the question.

750
00:48:05,000 --> 00:48:07,980
Jesus, what's with the birds?

751
00:48:09,140 --> 00:48:10,360
Matthew 13, 32.

752
00:48:10,360 --> 00:48:20,080
It's the smallest of all seeds, but when it's grown, it's taller than the garden plants and becomes a tree so that the birds of the sky will come and nest in its branches.

753
00:48:20,080 --> 00:48:23,600
Again, Jesus is not being literal here.

754
00:48:23,600 --> 00:48:27,160
He's tapping into the prophetic language of the Old Testament for his listeners.

755
00:48:28,040 --> 00:48:32,720
Especially Ezekiel 17 and Daniel 4, which Aaron read for us this morning.

756
00:48:32,720 --> 00:48:40,260
But real quick, Ezekiel 17, God plants a sprig from a cedar and it becomes a giant tree where birds of every kind find shelter.

757
00:48:40,260 --> 00:48:48,120
In Daniel 4, Nebuchadnezzar dreams of a tree so vast that it provides shelter for the beast and nesting places for the birds.

758
00:48:48,620 --> 00:48:59,280
See, in prophetic imagery, what Jesus is doing is he's using the birds to represent the nation, the outsiders, the unexpecting ones that are coming to the kingdom of heaven to find shelter.

759
00:48:59,280 --> 00:49:09,180
Jesus is hinting that the kingdom would grow in such a way that even the wrong type of people, the Gentiles, the sinners, the outsiders, would find a home in its branches.

760
00:49:09,180 --> 00:49:13,880
This is yet another scandalous, radical idea for his original audience.

761
00:49:13,880 --> 00:49:16,360
So what is Jesus doing here?

762
00:49:16,860 --> 00:49:19,960
He's doing what I say Jesus is always doing.

763
00:49:19,960 --> 00:49:23,160
And he's turning our understanding of power upside down.

764
00:49:23,160 --> 00:49:31,920
Instead of mighty cedars representing his royal empire, he compares his kingdom to a scrappy, unstoppable shrub.

765
00:49:31,920 --> 00:49:36,080
God starts small on purpose.

766
00:49:36,080 --> 00:49:38,100
Think about Jesus' life, right?

767
00:49:38,100 --> 00:49:42,520
Born in a backwater town to an unwed mother, no riches, no reputation, no political power.

768
00:49:42,520 --> 00:49:48,660
And yet, from his life, death, resurrection, and ascension grew a movement that changed the world.

769
00:49:48,660 --> 00:49:51,540
You and I are here today because of Jesus.

770
00:49:51,540 --> 00:49:57,960
The first century, or think about the 12 disciples, fishermen, tax collectors, nobodies.

771
00:49:58,820 --> 00:50:03,260
Yet, through them and through their testimony, the church was born.

772
00:50:03,260 --> 00:50:09,400
The first century church scattered, persecuted, hiding in homes, yet they grew.

773
00:50:09,400 --> 00:50:12,300
The church father, Tertullian, wrote,

774
00:50:12,780 --> 00:50:16,900
The blood of the martyrs is the seed of the church.

775
00:50:16,900 --> 00:50:21,660
All because a tiny seed was planted.

776
00:50:21,660 --> 00:50:25,760
And it rose up to overtake and fill the garden.

777
00:50:25,760 --> 00:50:30,680
When studying for this sermon, I came across an invasive tree in South Florida.

778
00:50:30,680 --> 00:50:31,960
The Australian pine.

779
00:50:32,080 --> 00:50:34,300
I don't know if we have any Floridians that are familiar with this.

780
00:50:34,300 --> 00:50:37,580
Once the seed takes root, it's nearly impossible to eradicate.

781
00:50:37,580 --> 00:50:40,040
Its roots spread deep and wide.

782
00:50:40,040 --> 00:50:40,700
You can cut it down.

783
00:50:40,700 --> 00:50:43,840
But unless you dig it up by the roots, it will come back.

784
00:50:43,840 --> 00:50:47,200
It's become a serious problem for city governments in Florida.

785
00:50:47,200 --> 00:50:52,100
And how do you control something so evasive, so persistent, so impossible to eradicate?

786
00:50:52,960 --> 00:50:58,100
And while reading that, I could not help but to think of the Roman government and the temple elites.

787
00:50:58,100 --> 00:51:03,940
They were trying to do this with Jesus and his followers, to cut them down, to uproot the movement,

788
00:51:03,940 --> 00:51:08,340
and bring power and control back to where the world says it should be.

789
00:51:08,340 --> 00:51:11,160
But they couldn't.

790
00:51:11,160 --> 00:51:12,840
The roots ran too deep.

791
00:51:12,840 --> 00:51:14,980
The seeds of the fruit spread too fast.

792
00:51:14,980 --> 00:51:18,140
And the kingdom of heaven was already taken over the garden.

793
00:51:18,140 --> 00:51:21,600
This is what the mustard seed looks like.

794
00:51:22,140 --> 00:51:24,200
Once it takes root, it is unstoppable.

795
00:51:24,200 --> 00:51:29,320
Friends, the kingdom of God is not fragile.

796
00:51:29,320 --> 00:51:31,360
It's not delicate.

797
00:51:31,360 --> 00:51:34,400
It does not depend on worldly power.

798
00:51:34,400 --> 00:51:37,760
Once planted, it will grow.

799
00:51:37,760 --> 00:51:40,800
But what's our job in that?

800
00:51:40,800 --> 00:51:41,600
Our vocation.

801
00:51:41,600 --> 00:51:50,180
We need to live and obey the king radically in service to his kingdom.

802
00:51:51,320 --> 00:51:52,360
So I'll ask you.

803
00:51:52,360 --> 00:51:57,440
Are you overlooking what God is doing because it looks so small?

804
00:51:57,440 --> 00:52:03,280
Is there a seed of God's word planted in you that you think is too tiny to matter?

805
00:52:03,280 --> 00:52:06,520
Friends, I would disciple you.

806
00:52:06,520 --> 00:52:09,380
Don't despise small beginnings.

807
00:52:10,720 --> 00:52:13,100
God does his best work beneath the soil.

808
00:52:13,100 --> 00:52:16,880
And remember, Jesus didn't just tell this story.

809
00:52:16,880 --> 00:52:17,280
He lived.

810
00:52:17,280 --> 00:52:21,680
The ultimate mustard seed moment was the death and resurrection of Jesus himself.

811
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:26,660
When the seed was planted into the ground, buried, dead, and forgotten by the world.

812
00:52:27,300 --> 00:52:31,580
But from that death sprang up the unstoppable life of the kingdom of God.

813
00:52:31,580 --> 00:52:35,960
Paul picks up the same picture in 1 Corinthians 15 when he talks about resurrection.

814
00:52:35,960 --> 00:52:39,720
What you sow does not come to life unless it dies.

815
00:52:39,720 --> 00:52:43,780
And what you sow is not the body that is to be, but a bare seed.

816
00:52:45,020 --> 00:52:46,820
Jesus' death was not defeat.

817
00:52:46,820 --> 00:52:48,120
It was planted.

818
00:52:48,120 --> 00:52:52,360
And his resurrection was the beginning of the great invasion of the kingdom.

819
00:52:52,360 --> 00:52:58,420
Just like a small seed overtakes the whole garden, the risen Christ is taking over the whole world.

820
00:52:59,380 --> 00:53:02,620
Church, this is how the kingdom of heaven works.

821
00:53:02,620 --> 00:53:06,780
Small beginnings, hidden growth, and unstoppable harvest.

822
00:53:06,780 --> 00:53:11,040
Jesus doesn't just leave us with that mustard seed.

823
00:53:11,040 --> 00:53:15,660
I think even 2,000 years ago, his listeners were probably as stubborn as we are.

824
00:53:15,660 --> 00:53:19,980
So he gives us another parable to drive the picture even deeper into our hearts.

825
00:53:19,980 --> 00:53:28,720
The kingdom of heaven is also like leaven that a woman took and hid in 50 pounds of flour until it was all leaven.

826
00:53:29,780 --> 00:53:32,980
All my girls and their bread-making arrows said, amen.

827
00:53:32,980 --> 00:53:37,400
But there's a tension here, right?

828
00:53:37,400 --> 00:53:41,380
There's a, there's a, want us to spot the problem.

829
00:53:41,380 --> 00:53:45,320
At first glance, this feels like a throwaway line.

830
00:53:45,320 --> 00:53:49,880
And I'm pretty sure I love confessing to things we're all probably guilty of, so that makes it a lot easier.

831
00:53:49,880 --> 00:53:51,560
But we've all read past this verse.

832
00:53:51,560 --> 00:53:56,500
It feels like something Jesus had to do to fill a required word count.

833
00:53:57,800 --> 00:54:00,760
It's short, it's domestic, it's quiet.

834
00:54:00,760 --> 00:54:06,400
Like that time we spent on the first part, I would disciple you not to let simplicity fool you.

835
00:54:06,400 --> 00:54:09,540
But this parable is also packed with punch.

836
00:54:09,540 --> 00:54:14,500
Leaven, yeast, it's active, it's alive.

837
00:54:14,500 --> 00:54:19,760
So when you mix a little bit of it into the dough, you can't see it anymore.

838
00:54:19,760 --> 00:54:20,880
Gone.

839
00:54:21,200 --> 00:54:28,140
But with some time and patience, the effects of that leaven are very evident in the dough.

840
00:54:28,140 --> 00:54:30,320
It is going to rise.

841
00:54:30,320 --> 00:54:32,140
It is going to expand.

842
00:54:32,140 --> 00:54:33,680
It may not be as pretty as you want it to be.

843
00:54:34,320 --> 00:54:38,980
But it's going to rise and it's going to expand and the leaven will work into every corner of the batch.

844
00:54:40,400 --> 00:54:43,380
That's what Jesus is saying the kingdom of heaven is like.

845
00:54:43,380 --> 00:54:48,320
Hidden, small, but powerfully transforming.

846
00:54:48,320 --> 00:54:53,200
Jesus is reinforcing the same theme that started with mustard seed.

847
00:54:53,200 --> 00:54:58,080
That God's kingdom may start in obscurity, but it may not look like much.

848
00:54:58,080 --> 00:55:00,840
But once it gets into the mix, you can't keep it from rising.

849
00:55:00,840 --> 00:55:02,800
You can't stop it from spreading.

850
00:55:02,800 --> 00:55:04,520
Here's the tension.

851
00:55:05,140 --> 00:55:07,200
And all my good church people will notice this tension.

852
00:55:07,200 --> 00:55:09,800
Yeast isn't always a good thing in the Bible.

853
00:55:09,800 --> 00:55:15,000
Actually, I'd say that overwhelmingly, yeast is portrayed as a negative symbol.

854
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:16,660
Something to be cautious of.

855
00:55:16,660 --> 00:55:18,660
So when you heard that, you were like, what do I do with that?

856
00:55:18,660 --> 00:55:23,740
In the Exodus narrative, God told Israel to remove the leaven from their houses during Passover

857
00:55:23,740 --> 00:55:26,200
because it represented Egypt and the old ways of life.

858
00:55:26,200 --> 00:55:29,740
In just three more chapters of Matthew, if you continue reading,

859
00:55:29,740 --> 00:55:33,060
Jesus will warn his disciples about the leaven of the Pharisees,

860
00:55:33,060 --> 00:55:34,900
about their hypocrisy and their corrupt teaching.

861
00:55:36,140 --> 00:55:41,620
Paul uses the symbol in 1 Corinthians 5 to describe how little sin can infect the whole church.

862
00:55:41,620 --> 00:55:44,480
So what is it Jesus is doing here?

863
00:55:44,480 --> 00:55:52,120
Is he flipping the symbol, using leaven to show the quiet power of the gospel?

864
00:55:52,120 --> 00:55:57,020
Or is it a subtle warning like, be careful what people are putting into the dough?

865
00:55:57,020 --> 00:55:59,300
Here's the beauty and tension.

866
00:55:59,300 --> 00:56:01,240
It might be both.

867
00:56:02,340 --> 00:56:06,100
On one hand, Jesus is saying the kingdom of heaven will rise.

868
00:56:06,100 --> 00:56:10,520
It may be hidden, it may seem small, but its influence is unstoppable.

869
00:56:10,520 --> 00:56:16,340
Like yeast, once the kingdom gets into the hearts of people or into the good soil of society,

870
00:56:16,340 --> 00:56:22,860
it goes to work quietly, powerfully, thoroughly because the kingdom of heaven is alive.

871
00:56:23,820 --> 00:56:27,700
But at the same time, there's a subtle echo here, a nudge to be alert, right?

872
00:56:27,700 --> 00:56:31,200
I think it's positive because Jesus starts at the kingdom of heaven is like.

873
00:56:31,200 --> 00:56:36,160
But I think there's a good reason to be hesitant here and to think through that.

874
00:56:36,160 --> 00:56:38,260
A nudge to be alert.

875
00:56:38,260 --> 00:56:39,440
Leaven is powerful.

876
00:56:39,440 --> 00:56:41,420
And folks, not all leaven is good.

877
00:56:42,420 --> 00:56:46,560
Not everything that spreads in the name of Jesus is actually from Jesus.

878
00:56:46,560 --> 00:56:50,040
I hate to break that truth to you this morning.

879
00:56:50,040 --> 00:56:59,540
But just like the kingdom can spread in hidden ways, so too can false teaching, hypocrisy, and compromise to the powers and principalities.

880
00:56:59,540 --> 00:57:01,600
And a little bit can go a long way.

881
00:57:03,180 --> 00:57:07,080
And church, again, confessing to you guys, I live in this tension.

882
00:57:07,080 --> 00:57:14,600
I live in this tension where I have a robust hope and optimism in the kingdom of God.

883
00:57:14,600 --> 00:57:21,780
But I also understand the warning about bad leaven and how it can also be at work.

884
00:57:21,780 --> 00:57:26,100
But rest assured, I believe that God is at work, even when we can't see it.

885
00:57:26,100 --> 00:57:27,540
Isaiah 55, 11 says,

886
00:57:27,680 --> 00:57:33,800
My word will not return to me empty, but will accomplish what I please and will prosper in what I send it to do.

887
00:57:33,800 --> 00:57:36,500
Good leaven is still at work.

888
00:57:36,500 --> 00:57:37,860
And it's still working today.

889
00:57:37,860 --> 00:57:40,660
Take a drink before I drop the hammer.

890
00:57:40,660 --> 00:57:45,600
You guys may not have me back, but that's okay.

891
00:57:45,600 --> 00:57:46,280
No, I'm just kidding.

892
00:57:46,280 --> 00:57:49,380
But here's what breaks my heart, church.

893
00:57:49,380 --> 00:57:54,460
When we don't have a kingdom theology and all we see is bad leaven.

894
00:57:57,680 --> 00:58:00,080
Man, times sure are bad.

895
00:58:00,080 --> 00:58:05,360
This world's going to hell in a handbasket.

896
00:58:05,360 --> 00:58:12,400
Yes, I will concede there is brokenness.

897
00:58:12,400 --> 00:58:13,580
There is darkness.

898
00:58:13,580 --> 00:58:17,720
There is false teaching, but no part of me is denying those facts.

899
00:58:17,720 --> 00:58:21,640
But if the world is dark, that is no time for the church to shrink back.

900
00:58:21,820 --> 00:58:27,620
It's time for the church to shine brighter, to be prophetic witnesses of our King, Jesus Christ,

901
00:58:27,620 --> 00:58:34,320
to call the powers of this world to account and to echo the same language that Jesus echoed to Pilate.

902
00:58:34,320 --> 00:58:40,300
You have no authority over me at all unless it's been given to you from above.

903
00:58:41,580 --> 00:58:49,380
Jesus is reminding Pilate where power truly resides, not in a Roman consul and not in a White House,

904
00:58:49,380 --> 00:58:52,640
but with the true King and his kingdom.

905
00:58:52,640 --> 00:58:57,420
Church, it's time we start living into our calling as kingdom people.

906
00:58:57,420 --> 00:59:02,200
The early church didn't retreat from the brokenness of this world, nor did they deny it.

907
00:59:02,860 --> 00:59:04,900
They marched forward in the name of Jesus.

908
00:59:04,900 --> 00:59:07,760
Where the church saw sickness, they created hospitals.

909
00:59:07,760 --> 00:59:12,840
Where they saw children with no one to love and care for them, they created orphanages.

910
00:59:12,840 --> 00:59:18,200
Where they saw image bearers of God cold and on the streets, they opened missions.

911
00:59:18,200 --> 00:59:23,860
And even participating with government, where they saw slavery, they appealed to Parliament.

912
00:59:23,860 --> 00:59:30,380
Where you see injustices, are you stepping into those injustices in the name of Jesus?

913
00:59:32,700 --> 00:59:40,200
Because I believe the kingdom of heaven is alive and active because every day I see individuals working for the kingdom because it's alive in them.

914
00:59:40,200 --> 00:59:45,600
Because I believe the risen Christ has overtaken the world through them.

915
00:59:45,600 --> 00:59:49,540
You may feel like your witness is unnoticed.

916
00:59:49,540 --> 00:59:51,420
That is a lie of the enemy.

917
00:59:51,420 --> 00:59:57,260
You may wonder if your prayers and your kindness and your faithfulness are making any real difference in this world.

918
00:59:57,260 --> 00:59:59,260
That is a lie of the enemy.

919
01:00:01,040 --> 01:00:08,560
The conversations you have, the acts of kindness, the quiet obedience, all in the name of Jesus is doing more than you and I could ever see.

920
01:00:08,560 --> 01:00:11,360
It's yeast moving through the dough.

921
01:00:11,360 --> 01:00:13,000
It's transforming hearts.

922
01:00:13,000 --> 01:00:17,500
It's bringing into focus for all that the kingdom of heaven is alive and breaking into this world.

923
01:00:17,500 --> 01:00:20,460
I want us to look at Jesus' own life again.

924
01:00:20,460 --> 01:00:22,580
Grew up in a no-name town.

925
01:00:22,580 --> 01:00:25,220
The disciples said, can anything good come from Nazareth?

926
01:00:26,160 --> 01:00:30,680
He preached to crowds, to hurting individuals, one broken life at a time.

927
01:00:30,680 --> 01:00:36,260
He called false witness and false teaching what it was, but invited them into a better way to live.

928
01:00:37,080 --> 01:00:37,980
He was rejected.

929
01:00:37,980 --> 01:00:39,340
He was crucified.

930
01:00:39,340 --> 01:00:41,980
He was buried in the ground like a seed.

931
01:00:41,980 --> 01:00:45,240
But on the third day, that seed cracked open.

932
01:00:45,240 --> 01:00:47,920
From that, the tree of life began to grow.

933
01:00:47,920 --> 01:00:54,040
From one crucified man to Christianity having a foothold in every major, every continent.

934
01:00:54,800 --> 01:00:59,180
From a manger to a throne, from the silence of the tomb to the roar of resurrection life.

935
01:00:59,180 --> 01:01:05,000
The risen Christ is still king, and he's still in the business of kingdom building.

936
01:01:05,000 --> 01:01:07,740
The seed is still breaking through the ground.

937
01:01:07,740 --> 01:01:10,080
The good yeast is still working its way through the dough.

938
01:01:10,080 --> 01:01:15,900
It's happening in homes, workplaces, classrooms, neighborhoods, prison rooms, hospital rooms,

939
01:01:15,900 --> 01:01:20,480
and places you and I will never see this side of eternity until one day we see it in full.

940
01:01:21,780 --> 01:01:22,900
But here's the challenge.

941
01:01:22,900 --> 01:01:26,820
Jesus said nobody lights a lamp and hides it under a bed.

942
01:01:26,820 --> 01:01:31,600
No, they set it high where they can give light to everyone around them.

943
01:01:31,600 --> 01:01:33,080
So what do we do?

944
01:01:33,080 --> 01:01:38,180
We plant the seeds, we mix in the good yeast, and we shine the light.

945
01:01:38,180 --> 01:01:42,560
We plant the seeds of the kingdom by sharing the good news with a friend,

946
01:01:42,560 --> 01:01:48,060
praying with and for co-workers, inviting the lonely to our table,

947
01:01:48,060 --> 01:01:50,700
choosing integrity when no one is watching,

948
01:01:51,360 --> 01:01:53,460
raising our children to know and love Jesus.

949
01:01:53,460 --> 01:02:00,320
We mix in good yeast into the dough by living quiet lives of obedience to Jesus,

950
01:02:00,320 --> 01:02:02,540
showing up in broken places,

951
01:02:02,540 --> 01:02:08,820
working for the justice, healing, and hope in the small corners where God has placed you and I.

952
01:02:08,820 --> 01:02:16,180
And coincidentally, we combat bad yeast by following the ways set forth by Jesus.

953
01:02:17,340 --> 01:02:20,020
And sometimes it will feel invisible.

954
01:02:20,020 --> 01:02:22,340
It will feel slow.

955
01:02:22,340 --> 01:02:25,920
It will feel like nothing is happening.

956
01:02:25,920 --> 01:02:28,920
But thank God the power isn't in us.

957
01:02:28,920 --> 01:02:30,700
The power is in our risen king.

958
01:02:31,300 --> 01:02:33,780
As Paul says in 1 Corinthians 3, 6,

959
01:02:33,780 --> 01:02:38,400
I planted, Apollos watered, but God gave the growth.

960
01:02:38,400 --> 01:02:41,020
You don't have to see it to believe it.

961
01:02:41,020 --> 01:02:43,180
You don't have to control it to believe it.

962
01:02:44,180 --> 01:02:46,100
And it doesn't have to be flashy to be faithful.

963
01:02:46,100 --> 01:02:53,620
Church, don't hide the hope you carry, the love you can give, and the grace you and I have to offer.

964
01:02:54,660 --> 01:02:55,920
You are not insignificant.

965
01:02:55,920 --> 01:02:59,820
The kingdom of heaven is at work through you.

966
01:02:59,820 --> 01:03:03,300
And I'll leave you with these thoughts from our parable today.

967
01:03:03,300 --> 01:03:05,600
I want you to value the small.

968
01:03:05,600 --> 01:03:08,640
Don't dismiss what seems insignificant.

969
01:03:08,640 --> 01:03:14,420
Your acts of kindness, your faithful prayers, your quiet obedience, they matter.

970
01:03:15,420 --> 01:03:18,080
God does big things with small seeds.

971
01:03:18,080 --> 01:03:21,620
Two, I want you to trust the process.

972
01:03:21,620 --> 01:03:26,000
Spiritual growth, cultural transformation, and healing.

973
01:03:26,000 --> 01:03:28,160
All these things take time.

974
01:03:28,160 --> 01:03:30,360
Trust the seed.

975
01:03:30,360 --> 01:03:32,020
Trust the kingdom.

976
01:03:32,020 --> 01:03:33,900
Trust God's time.

977
01:03:33,900 --> 01:03:37,540
I want you to be patient and faithful.

978
01:03:37,540 --> 01:03:41,660
It's good you don't see it doesn't mean it isn't growing.

979
01:03:41,660 --> 01:03:44,240
I want you to stay faithful in your part.

980
01:03:44,660 --> 01:03:45,940
No matter how small it feels.

981
01:03:45,940 --> 01:03:49,560
Four, I want you to be bold.

982
01:03:49,560 --> 01:03:51,860
The mustard seed is tiny.

983
01:03:51,860 --> 01:03:55,580
Once it's rooted, it is unstoppable.

984
01:03:55,580 --> 01:04:00,100
Don't be afraid to plant kingdom seeds in hard places.

985
01:04:00,100 --> 01:04:02,580
Because the kingdom of heaven is unstoppable.

986
01:04:02,580 --> 01:04:07,100
Five, you should be cautious of bad yeast.

987
01:04:07,100 --> 01:04:13,460
The enemy would love nothing more than for you to rally behind something.

988
01:04:13,900 --> 01:04:15,040
That is anti-Christ.

989
01:04:15,040 --> 01:04:25,080
The enemy would love nothing more than for us, the church, to rally behind something that is anti-Christ while convincing ourselves it's for Jesus.

990
01:04:27,740 --> 01:04:29,440
So, test everything.

991
01:04:29,440 --> 01:04:40,520
Every movement, every message, every impulse you and I have tested against the person, teachings, and life of Jesus.

992
01:04:41,980 --> 01:04:43,240
And don't do that alone.

993
01:04:43,240 --> 01:04:47,920
Do it with community, with believers who are grounded in Scripture and spirit.

994
01:04:50,340 --> 01:04:51,480
Don't waste your time.

995
01:04:51,480 --> 01:04:53,480
I can picture it in my Bible.

996
01:04:53,480 --> 01:05:00,880
Don't waste your time chasing conspiracy boards with yarn and thumbtacks, trying to map out every possible string theory.

997
01:05:01,720 --> 01:05:07,400
No, but instead, live into the real hope that is in Jesus Christ, our Lord.

998
01:05:07,400 --> 01:05:10,100
Let the light of the gospel shine in the shadows.

999
01:05:10,100 --> 01:05:13,260
Let the truth of his kingdom expose every counterfeit.

1000
01:05:14,140 --> 01:05:25,520
Jesus warns us of this in Matthew 24, 24, for false messiahs and false prophets will arise and perform great signs and wonders to lead astray, if possible, even the elect.

1001
01:05:27,320 --> 01:05:30,280
And last, I want you to be consistent.

1002
01:05:30,280 --> 01:05:39,100
Have you ever heard the story of someone who came to faith because of a long-forgotten seed planted years ago by a faithful kingdom worker?

1003
01:05:39,100 --> 01:05:47,760
Maybe that seed planter was a Sunday school teacher, a neighbor, a friend, or maybe just somebody that left a Bible on a shelf and you picked it up.

1004
01:05:47,760 --> 01:05:50,560
Maybe you're that recipient of the gospel.

1005
01:05:51,960 --> 01:05:55,880
A conversation from years ago still echoes in your heart even today.

1006
01:05:55,880 --> 01:06:04,020
A word of encouragement, a simple act of kindness, a lifelong friend who never gave up on you and continued to chase you down in the name of Jesus.

1007
01:06:04,020 --> 01:06:09,760
Jesus is and has worked through all those things to bring about transformation.

1008
01:06:09,760 --> 01:06:14,360
You never know how far the kingdom of God is spreading beneath the surface.

1009
01:06:14,360 --> 01:06:16,420
You and I are not the commander of the battlefield.

1010
01:06:16,420 --> 01:06:17,660
We are the followers.

1011
01:06:17,660 --> 01:06:21,420
I'll close today with Galatians 6, 9.

1012
01:06:21,960 --> 01:06:29,920
Let us not get tired of doing the good work, for we will reap at the prosper time if we don't give up.

1013
01:06:29,920 --> 01:06:31,420
Let's pray.

1014
01:06:31,420 --> 01:06:36,000
Father, in Jesus' name, we thank you for your kingdom.

1015
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:39,400
Hidden yet powerful, small yet unstoppable.

1016
01:06:39,400 --> 01:06:43,240
Help me to trust you in the small things.

1017
01:06:43,240 --> 01:06:50,480
To be faithful in the sowing of seeds and to believe in our hearts and actions that we proclaim your kingdom come,

1018
01:06:50,480 --> 01:06:53,320
your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

1019
01:06:53,320 --> 01:06:57,320
We pray all this for your glory and our neighbor's good.

1020
01:06:57,320 --> 01:06:58,300
Amen.

1021
01:07:12,220 --> 01:07:14,300
We're going to take communion here in just a minute.

1022
01:07:14,300 --> 01:07:20,040
If you didn't have a chance to grab it and you'd like to, just a reminder, we practice open communion at Canvas,

1023
01:07:20,040 --> 01:07:27,860
which means anyone who claims to have surrendered their life to Jesus is welcome to partake in it.

1024
01:07:27,860 --> 01:07:35,280
But there are strong warnings in the Bible that if you have not trusted in Jesus, this is not something for you to participate in.

1025
01:07:35,780 --> 01:07:38,120
So it's just something for you to observe.

1026
01:07:38,120 --> 01:07:47,400
I said last week after Kent's message that there's a part of me that's really excited about this sermon series,

1027
01:07:47,400 --> 01:07:49,140
and there's a part of me that's really anxious.

1028
01:07:50,340 --> 01:07:57,000
And I think the parable of the mustard seed and the parable of the yeast, which we don't call them that because we don't use names.

1029
01:07:57,000 --> 01:07:57,480
Sorry.

1030
01:07:57,480 --> 01:08:11,040
The two parables that we talked about today really communicate why I'm both very excited and anxious.

1031
01:08:11,040 --> 01:08:26,040
And that is, I think the American church, in the American church, we have, we've done a really good job of making the kingdom clean and neat and organized to appeal to a consumeristic group of people.

1032
01:08:26,040 --> 01:08:32,520
And I think we suffer from that as a church as well.

1033
01:08:32,520 --> 01:08:33,600
It's just in the air.

1034
01:08:34,260 --> 01:08:47,640
And as we really press into what Jesus says about the kingdom, there's going to be some things that we thought were true about the kingdom that we've embraced that feel good and make us feel warm inside and are comfy and cozy.

1035
01:08:47,640 --> 01:08:53,480
And Jesus is going to prophetically call us to lay those things down to follow what is true about his kingdom.

1036
01:08:55,280 --> 01:09:05,500
And I believe wholeheartedly that if we're willing to do that, it will lead to our good and our neighbor's good, but it'll be hard and it'll be scary.

1037
01:09:05,500 --> 01:09:09,520
So let's just keep coming back.

1038
01:09:09,520 --> 01:09:18,980
If you're brave, if you're bold, let's keep coming back and laying down our definition of God's kingdom at his feet and allow him to clarify it through his teachings.

1039
01:09:20,700 --> 01:09:26,080
Our parable today was about something seemingly small and insignificant that changed everything around it.

1040
01:09:26,080 --> 01:09:31,540
I think that would be a perfect way to describe the communion table.

1041
01:09:31,540 --> 01:09:47,260
To those outside the church, it's a humble table, the loaf of bread and a cup of wine or juice looks foolish, looks silly.

1042
01:09:48,640 --> 01:09:55,600
And yet throughout 2,000 years of history, it has the power to transform individuals from the inside out.

1043
01:09:55,600 --> 01:10:00,520
It's seemingly small and insignificant, but it's the place that can change everything.

1044
01:10:00,520 --> 01:10:05,300
The communion table is where those who are bitter find forgiveness.

1045
01:10:05,300 --> 01:10:09,700
It's where those who are crippled by shame can receive grace.

1046
01:10:09,700 --> 01:10:12,740
It's where the addicted can find freedom.

1047
01:10:13,980 --> 01:10:22,840
It's where diverse groups of people from every different cultural background can come together and find unity and surrender and love for Jesus.

1048
01:10:22,840 --> 01:10:25,260
It's where the poor are provided for.

1049
01:10:25,260 --> 01:10:26,480
It's where the lost are found.

1050
01:10:28,200 --> 01:10:34,600
The bread, the cup, the body, the blood can change everything.

1051
01:10:34,600 --> 01:10:43,740
So if you're a person of the kingdom, I'd invite you to take this wafer, Christ's body, broken for you.

1052
01:10:55,360 --> 01:10:57,180
Christ's blood shed for you.

1053
01:10:57,180 --> 01:11:14,380
Would you stand and join with me as we recite the Lord's Prayer on our way out?

1054
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:22,460
Whatever version you have memorized, if you don't have it memorized, just move your mouth and nobody beside you will know or judge you.

1055
01:11:24,660 --> 01:11:27,280
This is the prayer God gives us, Jesus gives us.

1056
01:11:27,280 --> 01:11:34,760
For kingdom people, our Father in heaven, holy is your name.

1057
01:11:34,760 --> 01:11:40,320
Your kingdom come, your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

1058
01:11:40,320 --> 01:11:43,100
Give us this day our daily bread.

1059
01:11:43,100 --> 01:11:48,300
Forgive our trespasses as we forgive those who trespass against us.

1060
01:11:49,100 --> 01:11:50,740
Lead us not into temptation.

1061
01:11:50,740 --> 01:11:52,700
Deliver us from evil.

1062
01:11:52,700 --> 01:11:57,960
For yours is the kingdom and the power and the glory forever and ever.

1063
01:11:57,960 --> 01:11:58,860
Amen.

1064
01:11:58,860 --> 01:12:01,860
Go in peace, church.

1065
01:12:01,860 --> 01:12:04,540
May the fourth be with you.

1066
01:12:12,620 --> 01:12:13,620
Amen.

1067
01:12:13,620 --> 01:12:15,620
Amen.

1068
01:12:42,620 --> 01:13:12,600
Thank you.

1069
01:13:12,620 --> 01:13:42,600
Thank you.

1070
01:13:42,620 --> 01:13:48,820
Thank you.
